  "caption": "Quinn signed up for a marathon, doubled the weekly distance by week 3, and by week 5 the shins and Achilles were complaining.\n\nCommon marathon-block injuries — shins, kneecap, ITB, Achilles — are often predictable: load rises faster than bone and tendon can adapt. Shoes and stretching usually aren't the main answer.\n\nWhat can help: raise weekly distance by 10% or less, add a lighter week after every three build weeks, avoid increasing distance and intensity together, strengthen calves and hips twice a week, and get any niggle lasting more than two weeks checked.\n\nGet it checked if one spot on the bone is very tender, pain builds during runs, or morning stiffness lasts more than 30 minutes.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
